    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L13-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Multiplying Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "On October 16, 1843, while walking across the Broom Bridge in Dublin, Ireland, Sir William Rowan Hamilton came up with an idea for numbers that would work sort of like complex numbers. Instead of just the number \\(i\\) (and its opposite…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L13-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Multiplying Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The way these numbers multiplied with each other was very interesting. \\(i\\) times \\(j\\) would give \\(k\\), \\(j\\) times \\(k\\) would give \\(i\\), and \\(k\\) times \\(i\\) would give \\(j\\). But the multiplication he imagined did not have a…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L13-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Multiplying Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Let \\(w=2+3i-j\\) and \\(z=2i+3k\\). Write each given expression in the form \\(a+bi+cj+dk\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L13-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Multiplying Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "To multiply two complex numbers, we use the distributive property:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L13-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Multiplying Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle (2 + 3i )(4 + 5i) = 8 + 10i + 12i + 15i^2\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L13-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Multiplying Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Remember that \\(i^2 = \\text- 1\\), so:",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L13-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Multiplying Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle (2 + 3i )(4 + 5i) = 8 + 10i + 12i - 15\\)",
